# Totem memory (trial, v1)

This project uses its own product: a shared, durable memory at
`https://totem-dev.fly.dev`. Workstation sessions, the hourly cloud routines,
and Cursor read and write the same store, so what one session saves is what
the next one starts with.

1. **Recall before reading.** Starting an advance, or touching a component
   you have not touched this session: recall first, on the advance id and the
   component names. A memory that contradicts a governance doc is the most
   valuable thing you will find.
2. **Save what the next session needs, not what you did.** Decisions and
   their reasoning, dead ends, corrections to specs, constraints discovered
   by running something. Never a summary of the diff — git has that.
3. **Default to `project:srswart/totem` scope.** Too narrow is invisible; too
   wide is noise for everyone.
4. **Give feedback when a memory helped or misled.** The value loop has no
   other way to learn.

Full detail — categories, what never to save, tool shapes — is in
`.claude/skills/totem-memory/SKILL.md`. It is written for Claude's skill
loader but reads as plain documentation.

**Cursor's remote-MCP reach is UNVERIFIED.** `docs/tech-direction/mcp.md`
records it as untested — the investigation sandbox could not reach Cursor's
documentation, and nothing has tested it since. If you are reading this in
Cursor and the Totem tools are not available, that is the known gap, not a
misconfiguration on your part.
